    "created_at": "2016-09-15T14:09:50Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-09-15T14:09:50Z",
    "body": "I talked about this a while back with @smaug----. https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-event-dispatch uses \"get the parent\" to determine where to invoke listeners. Something similar is used at the end of dispatch. https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=12230#c29 also explains this. That is what we should use here and we should only do it if the canceled flag is not set.\n\nThen we can let specifications define \"legacy post-dispatch steps\" for objects that need them (only `<a>`?). (I don't want to call it \"default action\", not even prefixed with \"legacy\". I think that would continue to cause much confusion.)\n\nDoes anyone see problems with that?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
