    "created_at": "2016-10-11T11:40:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-11T11:40:19Z",
    "body": "This basically means refactoring HTML too, for its \"run post-click activation steps\". I noticed HTML has \"run pre-click activation steps\" too, which are defined for `<input type=checkbox>` and `<input type=radio>`.\n\nAnd per http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4567 it seems these are run for all synthetic `click` events (as long as they implement the `MouseEvent` interface).\n\nSo maybe I should just integrate what HTML already defines, pre-click activation steps and activation behavior, and then update HTML to remove some of the redundancy. That seems like the easy way out here.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
