      "site_admin": false
    },
    "created_at": "2016-10-11T13:53:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-11T13:53:16Z",
    "body": "One thing we need to decide upon is when the post-click-dispatch steps are run. E.g., in Gecko the click event that causes those to be run will still have `eventPhase` set to 2, whereas in Chrome it is 0. http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4568\n\nBoth browsers do agree that `currentTarget` is null and only Chrome exposes `composedPath()` at the moment which returns an empty array.\n\nChrome also allows recursion to happen (stops after 42 times or so) whereas in Firefox the \"dispatch flag\" is not yet unset and therefore `dispatchEvent()` throws.\n\nI'm inclined to align with Chrome here though that would require taking a copy of event's path as we'd have to set it to null to not reveal anything through `composedPath()`.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/dom/issues/comments/252923107/reactions",
