    "created_at": "2016-10-12T10:48:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-12T10:48:49Z",
    "body": "There's another major difference between implementations here. It seems Chrome/Safari follow HTML when it comes to only running the pre/post steps for a single element, whereas Firefox does it for the entire event path. Simple demonstration: http://software.hixie.ch/utilities/js/live-dom-viewer/saved/4570. (What Chrome/Safari matches HTML's current language around \"activation behavior\" and seems better.)\n\n(Note that you cannot mutate the event path so you'll always get the same element.)\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
